{"id": "W3032345678", "title": "The impact of note-taking medium and review on recall", "year": 2020, "abstract": "Participants took notes by hand or laptop during a lecture and were randomly assigned to review or not review their notes. Laptop note takers recorded more words than longhand note takers. Reviewing notes improved recall for both groups, but the medium-by-review interaction was not significant. There was no evidence that review altered the relative effectiveness of handwritten versus laptop notes."}
